  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Ferric (59Fe) citrate is a radioactive form of iron citrate used as a diagnostic radiopharmaceutical. It is classed as experimental, so it is not an established marketed medicine and its current availability is unclear.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q27260867&quot;>Wikidata Q27260867</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>ferric (59Fe) citrate</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>V09XX04</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13582&quot;>DB13582</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:31605&quot;>31605</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q27260867&quot;>Q27260867</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C6H5FeO7</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>248.034 g/mol (Drugs.Common (25.09))</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
